---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="OCA Membership & Contributions | Why Ecosoft"
  description="Ecosoft is Thailand's only OCA member — the global standards body for open-source Odoo development. 120+ modules contributed to the international community."
>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">OCA Membership</p>
        <h1>The only Thai ERP partner that builds the platform — not just implements it.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          Ecosoft is Thailand's only OCA member and a certified ERPNext partner. We don't just
          implement the software — we contribute to building it. That depth is what makes our
          implementations different.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-metas">
          <div>
            <p class="metric-number">120+</p>
            <p class="metric-label">modules contributed</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="metric-number">1</p>
            <p class="metric-label">Thai OCA member</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="metric-number">10+</p>
            <p class="metric-label">years contributing</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-card">
        <div class="hero-card-main">
          <h2>What OCA membership means</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Rigorous peer review for all code contributions</li>
            <li>Automated testing on every module</li>
            <li>Documentation standards enforced globally</li>
            <li>International community validation</li>
            <li>Modules used by organisations worldwide</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-card-badges">
          <span>OCA Member</span>
          <span>Thailand — Only Member</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IS OCA -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; align-items: start;">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What is OCA</p>
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 1rem;">The global quality standard for open-source Odoo</h2>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            The Odoo Community Association (OCA) is the global standards body for open-source Odoo
            development. Founded in 2013, OCA sets the quality bar for all community Odoo modules —
            enforcing peer review, automated testing, and documentation standards that exceed most
            proprietary vendors.
          </p>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            Membership requires demonstrating sustained code quality and community contribution.
            Ecosoft is the only Thai company to have achieved OCA membership — a distinction that
            directly benefits every client we work with.
          </p>
          <p style="color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.95rem;">
            This matters to you because: the modules we implement are built to the highest quality
            standards in the world, tested by an international community of experts, and are free
            of proprietary lock-in by design.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
          <div class="info-card">
            <h3>🌍 Why OCA quality matters</h3>
            <p>OCA modules are used by thousands of organisations globally. The peer review process catches issues before they reach production. A module that passes OCA review is a module you can trust.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="info-card">
            <h3>🇹🇭 Thai advantage</h3>
            <p>No other Thai implementor contributes to OCA. That means our Thai localisation modules — withholding tax, VAT, 50 Tawi — are built to international standards and used by organisations across Thailand.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUR CONTRIBUTIONS -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our Contributions</p>
        <h2>120+ modules — built to the highest open-source standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every module Ecosoft contributes goes through the full OCA review process: peer code review,
          automated test suite, documentation, and compatibility verification across Odoo versions.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">🇹🇭</span>
          <h3>Thai Accounting Localisation</h3>
          <p>The definitive open-source Thai accounting suite: withholding tax, VAT reporting, 50 Tawi certificates, Thai chart of accounts, and BOI compliance — all contributed back to the global OCA community.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">📦</span>
          <h3>Supply Chain &amp; Procurement</h3>
          <p>Modules covering advanced procurement workflows, supplier evaluation, 3-way matching, and inventory management enhancements used by manufacturers and trading companies across Thailand.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">🏛️</span>
          <h3>Government ERP Modules</h3>
          <p>Purpose-built modules for Thai public sector compliance: government procurement, budget encumbrance, fund accounting, and contract management — tested in production at NSTDA, NXPO, HII, and BDI.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card pillar-card">
          <span class="pillar-number">⚙️</span>
          <h3>Frappe &amp; ERPNext Contributions</h3>
          <p>Active contributor to the ERPNext core and Frappe Framework — the foundation of ERPNext and the entire Frappe ecosystem. Our engineers work directly on the platform, not just on top of it.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY THIS MATTERS FOR YOUR PROJECT -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">What This Means for Your Project</p>
        <h2>Code quality you can verify — not just trust</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>✅ Peer-Reviewed Modules</h3>
          <p>Every module we implement has been reviewed by expert developers worldwide — not just internally. The standard is higher than most enterprise software vendors maintain.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>✅ Upgrade-Safe Customisations</h3>
          <p>OCA-standard modules are built to survive upgrades. When new versions of Odoo or ERPNext release, your customisations migrate cleanly — no expensive rewrites.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>✅ Community-Maintained</h3>
          <p>OCA modules are actively maintained by a global community. Even if Ecosoft didn't exist tomorrow, your modules would continue to be supported by hundreds of contributors.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>✅ Fully Auditable</h3>
          <p>All OCA repositories are public on GitHub. Your IT team, auditors, or any third-party developer can inspect every line of code we implement. No black boxes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem; text-align: center;">
        <a href="/resources/modules" class="btn btn-outline">View Our Module Library →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container cta-strip-grid">
      <div class="cta-strip-item">
        <h3>Want to understand what OCA means for your project?</h3>
        <p>Talk to our team — we can walk you through exactly which modules your implementation would use and how they're maintained.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-white">Talk to a Consultant</a>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-strip-item">
        <h3>See our open-source contributions</h3>
        <p>Browse the full library of modules Ecosoft has contributed to the global community.</p>
        <a href="/resources/modules" class="btn btn-teal-outline">Module Library →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
